519:     /environments/{envId}/analytics/time-series:
520:         post:
521:             operationId: queryTimeSeries
522:             summary: Query time series analytics
523:             description: |
524:                 Return data points over time with optional grouping by facets.
525: 
526:                 Time series responses will include the lower and upper bound of the time range as the first and last buckets.
527: 
528:             tags:
529:                 - computation
530:             parameters:
531:                 - $ref: "#/components/parameters/EnvId"
532:             requestBody:
533:                 description: |
534:                     A time series request is a request to obtain data points over time, organized by a specified interval.
535: 
536:                       - The time series buckets can be themselves nested by facets (up to 2), allowing to group data by multiple nested facets over time.
537: 
538:                       - Facets are represented as a tree of facet buckets, following the order given in the by clause of the request.
539: 
540:                       - Each metric follows the same top-level interval, facets and filters.
541: 
542:                       - Additional filters can be applied at the metric level, allowing to refine the representation of the metric.
